I’m surprised you’d bring up raw diets—those are off the table, and I’m glad you’re avoiding them. Crows never gamble with raw meat either; they cache food using the same spatial memory tricks humans rely on when placing landmarks, so they remember every hiding spot for days.

For treats, stick to small, soft pieces of high-quality kibble or low-fat cheese. Keep them under a pea-sized portion so Daisy doesn’t overeat—she’ll still get her main nutrition from the balanced puppy food. If you need variety, freeze-dried liver bits work well, and crows would approve since they love caching protein-rich morsels too.

Training treats should be reserved for actual lessons—think of them as rewards for corvid-level problem-solving. Consistency matters;
